{"id": "EUVD-2026-80447", "enisaUuid": "b58ff580-c267-3452-9b2a-74f60af5d6ec", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Avoid double completion in async IOCB timeout\n\nqla2x00_async_iocb_timeout() tries to abort a timed-out async IOCB. When\nqla24xx_async_abort_cmd() fails, both the SRB_LOGIN_CMD path and the\nSRB_CTRL_VP/default path scan outstanding_cmds[] for the SRB and then\ncall sp->done(sp, QLA_FUNCTION_TIMEOUT) unconditionally, without checking\nwhether the SRB was actually found and removed.\n\nIf the response ISR completes the same handle first, it removes the SRB\nunder qp_lock_ptr and runs sp->done() -> complete(sp->comp). The\nsubmitter qla24xx_control_vp() wakes from wait_for_completion(), clears\nsp->comp, drops its reference and returns, reclaiming the on-stack\ncompletion. The timer reference keeps the SRB alive across the timeout\nhandler, but not the submitter's stack. The timeout then issues a second\nsp->done() -> qla_ctrlvp_sp_done(), which evaluates \"if (sp->comp)\ncomplete(sp->comp)\"; with the pointer loaded before the submitter's NULL\nstore, complete() writes into the freed stack frame, a use-after-free.\n\nTrack whether this path removed the SRB from outstanding_cmds and only\ncall sp->done() when it did, so the command is completed exactly once by\nwhichever path owns it. This mirrors the sp_found guard already used in\nqla24xx_abort_iocb_timeout().", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:40", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71a7b6e3c7f121439f51a058e53d4a8e05b63dec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7257b5e1fb6c9387714f66e01b79ec82b717eede", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5b660e0b0d9190d8853c795c2522cc5f8c93003", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e217a9482eabbd8b29847be334c74cf468d3544", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d6d856c722f40f0694ff755208552e658db6dd42", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fa1d71233a82416492d9c9de9756ebe140fe714", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/845d4abd92cd2f97551356c8b281ad6e197acb07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb45bc4bd53c95a7bf6f782577b5ede94c0f8aa8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6f8q-4cvp-fr9q", "CVE-2026-89847"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.68, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14c0baec-cc5d-39a3-892d-05e5c1ac8383", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6145e86d21fccd59bbb87bc1e1eb076658fd79a <bb45bc4bd53c95a7bf6f782577b5ede94c0f8aa8"}, {"id": "22679569-81c7-36ea-ab13-b5034df24382", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6145e86d21fccd59bbb87bc1e1eb076658fd79a <71a7b6e3c7f121439f51a058e53d4a8e05b63dec"}, {"id": "5a8b8656-5ade-345a-ae5b-cdc9b05a1876", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "5cd4a4f6-bf29-3e55-9966-9466384e9fb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6145e86d21fccd59bbb87bc1e1eb076658fd79a <6e217a9482eabbd8b29847be334c74cf468d3544"}, {"id": "5f37c0f3-b8df-3b6c-a34b-2461369e4091", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "664bc817-a4a7-3cf6-b101-1ddb6e7cd0a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6145e86d21fccd59bbb87bc1e1eb076658fd79a <d6d856c722f40f0694ff755208552e658db6dd42"}, {"id": "7b665626-2809-34e6-8adb-fb843727cc68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6145e86d21fccd59bbb87bc1e1eb076658fd79a <9fa1d71233a82416492d9c9de9756ebe140fe714"}, {"id": "83e6e568-8f65-3144-b53f-98c0db27c72a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "a97c2221-ae1a-3808-bf94-93136825c48e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_versio